{"type":"text","timestamp":1788619893404,"sessionID":"ses_f8df3acbaffewojW0d3hVLR25n","part":{"id":"prt_0720d9f39001ZdMBwq3PMBsp5X","messageID":"msg_0720d9b320018uMjgugMCKneV0","sessionID":"ses_f8df3acbaffewojW0d3hVLR25n","type":"text","text":"I've analyzed the job and produced the task breakdown.\n\n## Analysis summary\n\n**Job:** `permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard` (branch verified via worktree path).\n\n**Problem:** `BottomSheetModal.svelte` (and the structurally identical `BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`) anchor the sheet to the bottom with `fixed ... h-dvh ... items-end`. On mobile the on-screen keyboard opens over the sheet because neither `dvh` nor `fixed` accounts for the keyboard — so the sheet's bottom (often its controls) is hidden.\n\n**Root cause & fix direction:** No `visualViewport`/keyboard handling exists anywhere in the codebase. The standard robust fix is to track `window.visualViewport` (`resize`/`scroll` in `onMount` with cleanup), compute keyboard height = `window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height`, and apply it as bottom padding on the overlay so the sheet lifts above the keyboard.\n\n**Scope findings:**\n- `ContentModal`, `QuickAddModal`, `MobileCalendarHeader` all delegate to `BottomSheetModal`, so fixing the shared component covers them.\n- `PopupContentModal`/`PopupConfirmationModal` are centered dialogs — out of scope.\n- No i18n strings affected.\n\n**Tasks produced (written to `tasks.md`):**\n- **TASK-1** (medium risk): keyboard-aware bottom offset in `BottomSheetModal.svelte` via VisualViewport API.\n- **TASK-2** (low risk): mirror the same fix in `BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`, depends on TASK-1.\n- **TASK-3** (low risk): `npm run check` verification, depends on TASK-1, TASK-2.\n\nNo human decision is required — the approach is well-established and scoped to the two bottom-sheet components. I did not modify any source code, only filled in the analyst `tasks.md` deliverable.","time":{"start":1788619890489,"end":1788619893402}}}
