{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788619970265,"sessionID":"ses_f8df14e3affe3wwrFMZEf9YPmr","part":{"id":"prt_0720ed6d6001Hl64JqIWQI8tvR","messageID":"msg_0720eca16001eC2HZDr66a9yUo","sessionID":"ses_f8df14e3affe3wwrFMZEf9YPmr","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788619971412,"sessionID":"ses_f8df14e3affe3wwrFMZEf9YPmr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6d8467b9582641eda7850ceb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: bottom sheet modal should sit above keyboard\n2: \n3: id: permission\n4: status: open\n5: analyst:\n6: date: 2026-09-05\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Context / finding\n11: \n12: `BottomSheetModal.svelte` (and the structurally identical `BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`)\n13: anchor the sheet to the bottom of the viewport with `fixed top-0 left-0 h-dvh w-screen flex items-end`.\n14: On mobile (PWA and the dedicated app shell) the on-screen keyboard opens over the sheet: neither `dvh`\n15: (which stays at the full layout-viewport height) nor `fixed` positioning accounts for the keyboard, so the\n16: sheet's bottom — often the interactive controls — is hidden underneath it.\n17: \n18: There is currently no `visualViewport` / keyboard handling anywhere in `src/`. The cleanest fix is to track\n19: the `window.visualViewport` and lift the sheet's bottom edge up by the keyboard height\n20: (`window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height`).\n21: \n22: Note: `ContentModal`, `QuickAddModal`, and `MobileCalendarHeader` all delegate to `BottomSheetModal`, so\n23: fixing the shared component covers them. `PopupContentModal` / `PopupConfirmationModal` are centered dialogs,\n24: not bottom sheets, and are out of scope.\n25: \n26: ## Task breakdown\n27: \n28: TASK-1: In `BottomSheetModal.svelte`, add a reactive keyboard-aware bottom offset: listen to\n29:      `window.visualViewport` `resize`/`scroll` in `onMount` (with proper cleanup), compute the keyboard\n30:      height as `max(0, window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height)`, and apply it as an inline\n31:      `padding-bottom` style on the overlay `<div>` so the sheet sits above the keyboard while keeping the\n32:      existing `pb-16 2xl:pb-0` classes as the no-keyboard default. Guard against counting normal browser\n33:      chrome / small jitter as a keyboard (only lift when the height difference exceeds a small threshold,\n34:      e.g. ~60px), and keep it SSR-safe (guarded to the client, no-op when `visualViewport` is unavailable,\n35:      e.g. desktop/older browsers).\n36:      files: src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetModal.svelte\n37:      depends: none\n38:      risk: medium — keyboard detection differs across iOS Safari / Chrome Android; threshold tuning and\n39:      listener lifecycle are the main pitfalls.\n40: \n41: TASK-2: Mirror the exact same keyboard-aware bottom-offset logic in `BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`,\n42:      which uses the identical `fixed ... h-dvh ... items-end` structure. If the developer finds the two\n43:      copies of the listener logic are drifting, extracting a tiny shared helper in `src/lib/helpers/` is\n44:      acceptable, but two small self-contained implementations are preferred over a new abstraction\n45:      (per the \"do not add abstractions not already present\" rule).\n46:      files: src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte\n47:      depends: TASK-1\n48:      risk: low — same change, second component; main risk is forgetting cleanup of the added listeners.\n49: \n50: TASK-3: Verify the change compiles cleanly with `npm run check` (and `npm run build` if feasible). No new\n51:      UI strings, so no i18n changes are expected. Manual on-device validation of keyboard behavior is the\n52:      only way to fully confirm the fix, but the code path is limited to the two bottom-sheet components.\n53:      files: none (verification only)\n54:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n55:      risk: low — type-check only; no new dependencies or strings.\n\n(End of file - total 55 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: bottom sheet modal should sit above keyboard\n\nid: permission\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-09-05\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context / finding\n\n`BottomSheetModal.svelte` (and the structurally identical `BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`)\nanchor the sheet to the bottom of the viewport with `fixed top-0 left-0 h-dvh w-screen flex items-end`.\nOn mobile (PWA and the dedicated app shell) the on-screen keyboard opens over the sheet: neither `dvh`\n(which stays at the full layout-viewport height) nor `fixed` positioning accounts for the keyboard, so the\nsheet's bottom — often the interactive controls — is hidden underneath it.\n\nThere is currently no `visualViewport` / keyboard handling anywhere in `src/`. The cleanest fix is to track\nthe `window.visualViewport` and lift the sheet's bottom edge up by the keyboard height\n(`window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height`).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: bottom sheet modal should sit above keyboard\n\nid: permission\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-09-05\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context / finding\n\n`BottomSheetModal.svelte` (and the structurally identical `BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`)\nanchor the sheet to the bottom of the viewport with `fixed top-0 left-0 h-dvh w-screen flex items-end`.\nOn mobile (PWA and the dedicated app shell) the on-screen keyboard opens over the sheet: neither `dvh`\n(which stays at the full layout-viewport height) nor `fixed` positioning accounts for the keyboard, so the\nsheet's bottom — often the interactive controls — is hidden underneath it.\n\nThere is currently no `visualViewport` / keyboard handling anywhere in `src/`. The cleanest fix is to track\nthe `window.visualViewport` and lift the sheet's bottom edge up by the keyboard height\n(`window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height`).\n\nNote: `ContentModal`, `QuickAddModal`, and `MobileCalendarHeader` all delegate to `BottomSheetModal`, so\nfixing the shared component covers them. `PopupContentModal` / `PopupConfirmationModal` are centered dialogs,\nnot bottom sheets, and are out of scope.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: In `BottomSheetModal.svelte`, add a reactive keyboard-aware bottom offset: listen to\n     `window.visualViewport` `resize`/`scroll` in `onMount` (with proper cleanup), compute the keyboard\n     height as `max(0, window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height)`, and apply it as an inline\n     `padding-bottom` style on the overlay `<div>` so the sheet sits above the keyboard while keeping the\n     existing `pb-16 2xl:pb-0` classes as the no-keyboard default. Guard against counting normal browser\n     chrome / small jitter as a keyboard (only lift when the height difference exceeds a small threshold,\n     e.g. ~60px), and keep it SSR-safe (guarded to the client, no-op when `visualViewport` is unavailable,\n     e.g. desktop/older browsers).\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetModal.svelte\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — keyboard detection differs across iOS Safari / Chrome Android; threshold tuning and\n     listener lifecycle are the main pitfalls.\n\nTASK-2: Mirror the exact same keyboard-aware bottom-offset logic in `BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`,\n     which uses the identical `fixed ... h-dvh ... items-end` structure. If the developer finds the two\n     copies of the listener logic are drifting, extracting a tiny shared helper in `src/lib/helpers/` is\n     acceptable, but two small self-contained implementations are preferred over a new abstraction\n     (per the \"do not add abstractions not already present\" rule).\n     files: src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: low — same change, second component; main risk is forgetting cleanup of the added listeners.\n\nTASK-3: Verify the change compiles cleanly with `npm run check` (and `npm run build` if feasible). No new\n     UI strings, so no i18n changes are expected. Manual on-device validation of keyboard behavior is the\n     only way to fully confirm the fix, but the code path is limited to the two bottom-sheet components.\n     files: none (verification only)\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n     risk: low — type-check only; no new dependencies or strings.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":55,"totalLines":55,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/tasks.md","time":{"start":1788619971402,"end":1788619971410}},"id":"prt_0720ed9e5001P1uPjs1I2IAUV0","sessionID":"ses_f8df14e3affe3wwrFMZEf9YPmr","messageID":"msg_0720eca16001eC2HZDr66a9yUo"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788619971696,"sessionID":"ses_f8df14e3affe3wwrFMZEf9YPmr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_21ebb0ae0f4b4e7da3184951","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: Fixed the bottom-sheet modals being hidden underneath the on-screen keyboard on\n4: mobile (PWA / dedicated app). Both bottom-sheet components now track\n5: `window.visualViewport` and lift their bottom edge up by the keyboard height so\n6: the sheet — and its interactive controls — remain visible above the keyboard.\n7: \n8: ## Changes\n9: \n10: TASK-1 (`src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetModal.svelte`):\n11: - Added an `onMount` that listens to `window.visualViewport` `resize`/`scroll`\n12:   events (with proper cleanup on destroy).\n13: - Computes `keyboardHeight = max(0, window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height)`\n14:   and only applies it when the difference exceeds a 60px threshold (to avoid\n15:   counting normal browser chrome / small jitter as a keyboard).\n16: - Applies the result as an inline `style:padding-bottom` on the overlay div,\n17:   keeping the existing `pb-16 2xl:pb-0` classes as the no-keyboard default.\n18: - SSR-safe: guarded to the client, no-op when `visualViewport` is unavailable.\n19: - `ContentModal`, `QuickAddModal`, and `MobileCalendarHeader` delegate to this\n20:   component, so they are covered automatically.\n21: \n22: TASK-2 (`src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`):\n23: - Mirrored the exact same keyboard-aware bottom-offset logic (identical\n24:   structure/guard/threshold). Two small self-contained implementations kept, as\n25:   preferred over a new shared abstraction.\n26: \n27: TASK-3 (verification):\n28: - Could not run `npm run check` / `npm run build` because `node_modules` is not\n29:   installed in this environment (and installing dependencies is disallowed\n30:   without confirmation). Changes are minimal and self-contained; the two\n31:   components are now structurally consistent.\n32: \n33: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n34: \n35: - Manual on-device validation (iOS Safari / Chrome Android) is the only way to\n36:   fully confirm keyboard behavior across platforms; the threshold (60px) and\n37:   `visualViewport` behavior may need tuning on specific devices.\n38: - `PopupContentModal` / `PopupConfirmationModal` are centered dialogs and were\n39:   intentionally left out of scope.\n\n(End of file - total 39 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nFixed the bottom-sheet modals being hidden underneath the on-screen keyboard on\nmobile (PWA / dedicated app). Both bottom-sheet components now track\n`window.visualViewport` and lift their bottom edge up by the keyboard height so\nthe sheet — and its interactive controls — remain visible above the keyboard.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1 (`src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetModal.svelte`):\n- Added an `onMount` that listens to `window.visualViewport` `resize`/`scroll`\n  events (with proper cleanup on destroy).\n- Computes `keyboardHeight = max(0, window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height)`\n  and only applies it when the difference exceeds a 60px threshold (to avoid\n  counting normal browser chrome / small jitter as a keyboard).\n- Applies the result as an inline `style:padding-bottom` on the overlay div,\n  keeping the existing `pb-16 2xl:pb-0` classes as the no-keyboard default.\n- SSR-safe: guarded to the client, no-op when `visualViewport` is unavailable.\n- `ContentModal`, `QuickAddModal`, and `MobileCalendarHeader` delegate to this\n  component, so they are covered automatically.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed the bottom-sheet modals being hidden underneath the on-screen keyboard on\nmobile (PWA / dedicated app). Both bottom-sheet components now track\n`window.visualViewport` and lift their bottom edge up by the keyboard height so\nthe sheet — and its interactive controls — remain visible above the keyboard.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1 (`src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetModal.svelte`):\n- Added an `onMount` that listens to `window.visualViewport` `resize`/`scroll`\n  events (with proper cleanup on destroy).\n- Computes `keyboardHeight = max(0, window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height)`\n  and only applies it when the difference exceeds a 60px threshold (to avoid\n  counting normal browser chrome / small jitter as a keyboard).\n- Applies the result as an inline `style:padding-bottom` on the overlay div,\n  keeping the existing `pb-16 2xl:pb-0` classes as the no-keyboard default.\n- SSR-safe: guarded to the client, no-op when `visualViewport` is unavailable.\n- `ContentModal`, `QuickAddModal`, and `MobileCalendarHeader` delegate to this\n  component, so they are covered automatically.\n\nTASK-2 (`src/lib/components/ui/BottomSheetConfirmationModal.svelte`):\n- Mirrored the exact same keyboard-aware bottom-offset logic (identical\n  structure/guard/threshold). Two small self-contained implementations kept, as\n  preferred over a new shared abstraction.\n\nTASK-3 (verification):\n- Could not run `npm run check` / `npm run build` because `node_modules` is not\n  installed in this environment (and installing dependencies is disallowed\n  without confirmation). Changes are minimal and self-contained; the two\n  components are now structurally consistent.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Manual on-device validation (iOS Safari / Chrome Android) is the only way to\n  fully confirm keyboard behavior across platforms; the threshold (60px) and\n  `visualViewport` behavior may need tuning on specific devices.\n- `PopupContentModal` / `PopupConfirmationModal` are centered dialogs and were\n  intentionally left out of scope.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":39,"totalLines":39,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/permission_bottom-sheet-modal-should-sit-above-keyboard/implementation.md","time":{"start":1788619971687,"end":1788619971694}},"id":"prt_0720edb660013vuFtAynM0zF2E","sessionID":"ses_f8df14e3affe3wwrFMZEf9YPmr","messageID":"msg_0720eca16001eC2HZDr66a9yUo"}}
